<hr data-start=3D"3968" data-end=3D"3971">
<h1 data-start=3D"3973" data-end=3D"4022">6) Important properties, pros and=
 cons (simple)</h1>
<p data-start=3D"4023" data-end=3D"4031"><strong data-start=3D"4023" data-e=
nd=3D"4031">Pros</strong></p>
<ul data-start=3D"4032" data-end=3D"4164">
<li data-start=3D"4032" data-end=3D"4054">
<p data-start=3D"4034" data-end=3D"4054">Simple to implement.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4055" data-end=3D"4098">
<p data-start=3D"4057" data-end=3D"4098">Fast in practice for moderate size=
d data.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4099" data-end=3D"4164">
<p data-start=3D"4101" data-end=3D"4164">Works well when clusters are spher=
ical / separated by distance.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"4166" data-end=3D"4184"><strong data-start=3D"4166" data-e=
nd=3D"4184">Cons / gotchas</strong></p>
<ul data-start=3D"4185" data-end=3D"4732">
<li data-start=3D"4185" data-end=3D"4256">
<p data-start=3D"4187" data-end=3D"4256"><strong data-start=3D"4187" data-e=
nd=3D"4198">Needs k</strong>: you must choose the number of clusters <span =
class=3D"katex"><span class=3D"katex-mathml"><math xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.o=
rg/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=
=3D"application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=
=3D"katex-html" aria-hidden=3D"true"><span class=3D"base"><span class=3D"st=
rut" style=3D"height: 0.6944em;"></span><span class=3D"mord mathnormal" sty=
le=3D"margin-right: 0.03148em;">k</span></span></span></span> in advance.</=
p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4257" data-end=3D"4438">
<p data-start=3D"4259" data-end=3D"4438"><strong data-start=3D"4259" data-e=
nd=3D"4285">Initialization matters</strong>: different random starts can le=
ad to different final clusters (local minima). Use multiple starts or smart=
er initializers (like k-means++), if possible.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4439" data-end=3D"4565">
<p data-start=3D"4441" data-end=3D"4565"><strong data-start=3D"4441" data-e=
nd=3D"4486">Only finds Euclidean, mean-based clusters</strong>: it minimize=
s SSE, not necessarily what you intuitively want for other shapes.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4566" data-end=3D"4630">
<p data-start=3D"4568" data-end=3D"4630"><strong data-start=3D"4568" data-e=
nd=3D"4593">Sensitive to outliers</strong>: means get pulled by extreme val=
ues.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4631" data-end=3D"4732">
<p data-start=3D"4633" data-end=3D"4732"><strong data-start=3D"4633" data-e=
nd=3D"4650">Cluster sizes</strong>: favors clusters of similar variance; tr=
icky when cluster densities/sizes differ.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"4734" data-end=3D"4737">
<h1 data-start=3D"4739" data-end=3D"4765">7) When K-means finishes</h1>
<ul data-start=3D"4766" data-end=3D"4968">
<li data-start=3D"4766" data-end=3D"4897">
<p data-start=3D"4768" data-end=3D"4897">The algorithm ends when centroids =
stop moving (the change is below some small <span class=3D"katex"><span cla=
ss=3D"katex-mathml"><math xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><sem=
antics><mrow><mi>=CF=B5</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=3D"application/x-te=
x">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=3D"katex-html=
" aria-hidden=3D"true"><span class=3D"base"><span class=3D"strut" style=3D"=
height: 0.4306em;"></span><span class=3D"mord mathnormal">=CF=B5</span></sp=
an></span></span>), or after a set number of iterations.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4898" data-end=3D"4968">
<p data-start=3D"4900" data-end=3D"4968">The result is a local minimum of S=
SE, not guaranteed global minimum.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"4970" data-end=3D"4973">
<h1 data-start=3D"4975" data-end=3D"4994">8) Practical tips</h1>
<ul data-start=3D"4995" data-end=3D"5316">
<li data-start=3D"4995" data-end=3D"5082">
<p data-start=3D"4997" data-end=3D"5082">Standardize features (zero mean, u=
nit variance) when dimensions have different units.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5083" data-end=3D"5166">
<p data-start=3D"5085" data-end=3D"5166">Run K-means several times with dif=
ferent initial centroids and pick the best SSE.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5167" data-end=3D"5230">
<p data-start=3D"5169" data-end=3D"5230">Use heuristics (elbow method, silh=
ouette) to help pick <span class=3D"katex"><span class=3D"katex-mathml"><ma=
th xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi>=
</mrow><annotation encoding=3D"application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics=
></math></span><span class=3D"katex-html" aria-hidden=3D"true"><span class=
=3D"base"><span class=3D"strut" style=3D"height: 0.6944em;"></span><span cl=
ass=3D"mord mathnormal" style=3D"margin-right: 0.03148em;">k</span></span><=
/span></span>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5231" data-end=3D"5316">
<p data-start=3D"5233" data-end=3D"5316">For better initialization use <str=
ong data-start=3D"5263" data-end=3D"5276">k-means++</strong> (it spreads in=
itial centroids smartly).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"5318" data-end=3D"5321">
<h1 data-start=3D"5323" data-end=3D"5346">Short summary =E2=80=94 TL;DR</h1=
>
