se dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-=
start=3D"0" data-end=3D"254">Perfect =E2=80=94 I=E2=80=99ll walk you throug=
h <strong data-start=3D"32" data-end=3D"56">K-means step-by-step</strong> i=
n the <em data-start=3D"64" data-end=3D"74">simplest</em> possible way so y=
ou really understand what=E2=80=99s happening. I=E2=80=99ll use the same sm=
all 1-D example (so you can do every calculation by hand) and show each ari=
thmetic step digit-by-digit.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"256" data-end=3D"259">
<h2 data-start=3D"261" data-end=3D"287">The setup (very simple)</h2>
<p data-start=3D"288" data-end=3D"364">Dataset (points on a number line):<b=
r data-start=3D"322" data-end=3D"325">
<code data-start=3D"325" data-end=3D"364">D =3D [2, 3, 4, 10, 11, 12, 20, 2=
5, 30]</code></p>
<p data-start=3D"366" data-end=3D"391">We want <code data-start=3D"374" dat=
a-end=3D"381">k =3D 2</code> clusters.</p>
<p data-start=3D"393" data-end=3D"615">Think of centroids as <strong data-s=
tart=3D"415" data-end=3D"435">two post offices</strong>. Every house (data =
point) goes to the nearest post office. Then each post office moves to the =
average location of all houses assigned to it. Repeat until post offices st=
op moving.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"617" data-end=3D"620">
<h2 data-start=3D"622" data-end=3D"654">The algorithm (short &amp; plain)</=
h2>
<p data-start=3D"655" data-end=3D"662">Repeat:</p>
<ol data-start=3D"663" data-end=3D"897">
<li data-start=3D"663" data-end=3D"768">
<p data-start=3D"666" data-end=3D"768"><strong data-start=3D"666" data-end=
=3D"676">Assign</strong> each point to the cluster whose centroid is closes=
t (distance =3D absolute difference in 1D).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"769" data-end=3D"897">
<p data-start=3D"772" data-end=3D"897"><strong data-start=3D"772" data-end=
=3D"782">Update</strong> each centroid =3D the mean (average) of points ass=
igned to it.<br>
Stop when centroids don=E2=80=99t change (or change is tiny).</p>
</li>
</ol>
<hr data-start=3D"899" data-end=3D"902">
<h2 data-start=3D"904" data-end=3D"938">Start: choose initial centroids</h2=
>
<p data-start=3D"939" data-end=3D"1025">We pick initial centroids (you can =
choose randomly or by heuristic).<br>
Let=E2=80=99s start with:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"1026" data-end=3D"1048">
<li data-start=3D"1026" data-end=3D"1036">
<p data-start=3D"1028" data-end=3D"1036"><code data-start=3D"1028" data-end=
=3D"1036">=CE=BC1 =3D 2</code></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1037" data-end=3D"1048">
<p data-start=3D"1039" data-end=3D"1048"><code data-start=3D"1039" data-end=
=3D"1048">=CE=BC2 =3D 25</code></p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"1050" data-end=3D"1053">
<h2 data-start=3D"1055" data-end=3D"1125">Iteration 1 =E2=80=94 Cluster ass=
ignment (compute distances digit-by-digit)</h2>
<p data-start=3D"1127" data-end=3D"1219">We compute distance from each poin=
t <code data-start=3D"1163" data-end=3D"1166">x</code> to <code data-start=
=3D"1170" data-end=3D"1174">=CE=BC1</code> and <code data-start=3D"1179" da=
ta-end=3D"1183">=CE=BC2</code> and assign to the smaller distance.</p>
<ol data-start=3D"1221" data-end=3D"2163">
<li data-start=3D"1221" data-end=3D"1354">
<p data-start=3D"1224" data-end=3D"1236">For <code data-start=3D"1228" data=
-end=3D"1235">x =3D 2</code>:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"1240" data-end=3D"1354">
<li data-start=3D"1240" data-end=3D"1266">
<p data-start=3D"1242" data-end=3D"1266"><code data-start=3D"1242" data-end=
=3D"1266">|2 - =CE=BC1| =3D |2 - 2| =3D 0</code></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1270" data-end=3D"1354">
<p data-start=3D"1272" data-end=3D"1354"><code data-start=3D"1272" data-end=
=3D"1298">|2 - =CE=BC2| =3D |2 - 25| =3D 23</code><br>
=E2=86=92 nearest: <code data-start=3D"1313" data-end=3D"1317">=CE=BC1</cod=
e> (since 0 &lt; 23). Assign 2 =E2=86=92 cluster1.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1356" data-end=3D"1452">
<p data-start=3D"1359" data-end=3D"1371">For <code data-start=3D"1363" data=
-end=3D"1370">x =3D 3</code>:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"1375" data-end=3D"1452">
<li data-start=3D"1375" data-end=3D"1390">
<p data-start=3D"1377" data-end=3D"1390"><code data-start=3D"1377" data-end=
=3D"1390">|3 - 2| =3D 1</code></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1394" data-end=3D"1452">
<p data-start=3D"1396" data-end=3D"1452"><code data-start=3D"1396" data-end=
=3D"1411">|3 - 25| =3D 22</code><br>
=E2=86=92 nearest: <code data-start=3D"1426" data-end=3D"1430">=CE=BC1</cod=
e>. Assign 3 =E2=86=92 cluster1.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
