d=3D"3670">C2 =3D {20,25,30}</code>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"3673" data-end=3D"3771">Because the cluster memberships st=
ayed the same, recomputing centroids will give the same results:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"3772" data-end=3D"3807">
<li data-start=3D"3772" data-end=3D"3807">
<p data-start=3D"3774" data-end=3D"3807">=CE=BC1 =3D 7, =CE=BC2 =3D 25 (sam=
e as before).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"3809" data-end=3D"3869"><strong data-start=3D"3809" data-e=
nd=3D"3822">Converged</strong> (no change in centroids or assignments). Don=
e.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"3871" data-end=3D"3874">
<h2 data-start=3D"3876" data-end=3D"3910">Final result (easy to remember)</=
h2>
<ul data-start=3D"3911" data-end=3D"4032">
<li data-start=3D"3911" data-end=3D"4032">
<p data-start=3D"3913" data-end=3D"4032">Final clusters:<br data-start=3D"3=
928" data-end=3D"3931">
<code data-start=3D"3933" data-end=3D"3961">C1 =3D {2, 3, 4, 10, 11, 12}</c=
ode> with centroid <code data-start=3D"3976" data-end=3D"3984">=CE=BC1 =3D =
7</code><br data-start=3D"3984" data-end=3D"3987">
<code data-start=3D"3989" data-end=3D"4008">C2 =3D {20, 25, 30}</code> with=
 centroid <code data-start=3D"4023" data-end=3D"4032">=CE=BC2 =3D 25</code>=
</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"4034" data-end=3D"4037">
<h2 data-start=3D"4039" data-end=3D"4076">Why this makes sense (intuitively=
)</h2>
<ul data-start=3D"4077" data-end=3D"4511">
<li data-start=3D"4077" data-end=3D"4163">
<p data-start=3D"4079" data-end=3D"4163">Each point goes to the closest cen=
troid =E2=80=94 simple nearest neighbor in centroid space.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4164" data-end=3D"4274">
<p data-start=3D"4166" data-end=3D"4274">The centroid is the average of its=
 points =E2=80=94 the mean minimizes the sum of squared distances to those =
points.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4275" data-end=3D"4380">
<p data-start=3D"4277" data-end=3D"4380">After assignment, moving centroid =
to the mean reduces the SSE (sum of squared errors) for that cluster.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4381" data-end=3D"4511">
<p data-start=3D"4383" data-end=3D"4511">Iterating these two steps reduces =
SSE overall and eventually gets to a point where moving centroids further d=
oesn=E2=80=99t improve SSE.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"4513" data-end=3D"4516">
<h2 data-start=3D"4518" data-end=3D"4570">Key ideas to lock into your brain=
 (short bullets)</h2>
<ul data-start=3D"4571" data-end=3D"4969">
<li data-start=3D"4571" data-end=3D"4636">
<p data-start=3D"4573" data-end=3D"4636"><strong data-start=3D"4573" data-e=
nd=3D"4598">Two alternating steps</strong>: assign =E2=86=92 update =E2=86=
=92 assign =E2=86=92 update...</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4637" data-end=3D"4731">
<p data-start=3D"4639" data-end=3D"4731"><strong data-start=3D"4639" data-e=
nd=3D"4670">Distance decides assignment</strong> (in 1D, absolute differenc=
e; in multi-D, usually Euclidean).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4732" data-end=3D"4802">
<p data-start=3D"4734" data-end=3D"4802"><strong data-start=3D"4734" data-e=
nd=3D"4769">Mean is the best representative</strong> for minimizing squared=
 distance.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4803" data-end=3D"4852">
<p data-start=3D"4805" data-end=3D"4852"><strong data-start=3D"4805" data-e=
nd=3D"4835">Stops when nothing changes</strong> (local minimum).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4853" data-end=3D"4934">
<p data-start=3D"4855" data-end=3D"4934"><strong data-start=3D"4855" data-e=
nd=3D"4881">Initialization matters</strong>: different starts can give diff=
erent final clusters.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4935" data-end=3D"4969">
<p data-start=3D"4937" data-end=3D"4969"><strong data-start=3D"4937" data-e=
nd=3D"4968">k must be chosen beforehand</strong>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"4971" data-end=3D"4974">
<h2 data-start=3D"4976" data-end=3D"5052">Quick mental checks / mini-exerci=
ses (practice to strengthen the concept)</h2>
<ol data-start=3D"5053" data-end=3D"5369">
<li data-start=3D"5053" data-end=3D"5189">
<p data-start=3D"5056" data-end=3D"5189">Try different initial centroids (e=
.g., =CE=BC1 =3D 3, =CE=BC2 =3D 20). See how many iterations until converge=
nce and whether final clusters change.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5190" data-end=3D"5292">
<p data-start=3D"5193" data-end=3D"5292">Add an outlier (e.g., point <code =
data-start=3D"5221" data-end=3D"5226">100</code>) and see how centroids mov=
e =E2=80=94 that shows sensitivity to outliers.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5293" data-end=3D"5369">
<p data-start=3D"5296" data-end=3D"5369">Try <code data-start=3D"5300" data=
-end=3D"5307">k =3D 3</code> on the same data and see how the algorithm spl=
its the points.</p>
</li>
</ol>
